<h3>Build and stability</h3>
<p>The lighter frame is the biggest trade-off. It makes the machine easy to lift and store, but it also means the base can creep forward as you push, especially on hardwood or tile. A [[amazon:cubii-mat|non-slip mat]] solves most of this. Owners who pedal at an easy pace report fewer problems than those who push hard at high resistance.</p>

<h3>Resistance and effort</h3>
<p>The resistance range is aimed at light to moderate effort. That is fine for typing and reading, where you want to move without breaking focus. If you want to feel your quads burn, look at the models in our <a href="/under-desk-elliptical-with-resistance/">under desk elliptical with resistance</a> guide.</p>

